# US economic time series: economics

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

ggplot2's reference page for [`economics`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/economics.html),
which covers `economics_long` too, has no examples, so this notebook says only what the page
describes and where Giggly stands.

`economics` holds US economic time series from the data published at fred.stlouisfed.org: for
each of 574 months, personal consumption expenditures, the total population, the personal savings
rate, the median duration of unemployment and the number of people unemployed. `economics` is in
wide format, a column per series; `economics_long` holds the same series in long format, a row per
month and series, with each series also rescaled to run from 0 to 1, in `value01`, so all five can
share an axis. `Giggly.Datasets.economics/0` is `economics` and `Giggly.Datasets.economics_long/0`
is `economics_long`, their `date` columns dates, which Giggly puts on an axis as ggplot2 does.
